WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.874 --> 00:00:02.917
Line 3 runs in hall B.

2
00:00:03.597 --> 00:00:08.346
Now a new MES is coming, the system that runs the orders on the floor.

3
00:00:09.363 --> 00:00:11.836
You lead that IT project for the plant manager.

4
00:00:12.566 --> 00:00:15.109
The IT team builds the MES.

5
00:00:16.192 --> 00:00:17.887
That takes four stations.

6
00:00:18.621 --> 00:00:22.662
Short cycles, many teams, safe delivery and leading the project.

7
00:00:23.989 --> 00:00:26.497
The first station is Agile and Scrum.

8
00:00:27.196 --> 00:00:31.816
The IT team builds the MES in short rounds, called sprints.

9
00:00:32.815 --> 00:00:35.311
After each round users try it out.

10
00:00:36.148 --> 00:00:37.588
Then the team adjusts.

11
00:00:38.586 --> 00:00:41.117
You use a Kanban board and planning poker.

12
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:46.214
Without this you only find out after months that you built the wrong thing.

13
00:00:47.511 --> 00:00:50.623
The second station is Scaling, SAFe and beyond.

14
00:00:51.397 --> 00:00:54.392
One team is too small for the whole MES.

15
00:00:55.456 --> 00:00:59.182
Then the teams plan together and work to one rhythm, like a train.

16
00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:03.003
You use PI Planning and WSJF.

17
00:01:04.032 --> 00:01:07.944
Without this the whole gets stuck, because one team waits for another.

18
00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:11.995
The third station is DevOps and delivery.

19
00:01:12.673 --> 00:01:16.040
Whoever builds the MES also keeps it running.

20
00:01:17.036 --> 00:01:20.403
A new version goes through test and acceptance first.

21
00:01:21.162 --> 00:01:23.147
Only then does it go to the floor.

22
00:01:24.187 --> 00:01:26.590
You use a pipeline and a feature flag.

23
00:01:27.591 --> 00:01:32.501
Without this every step stays manual, and that is where errors and waiting arise.

24
00:01:33.812 --> 00:01:36.773
The fourth station is Leading IT projects.

25
00:01:37.458 --> 00:01:39.826
From requirements and vendor to go-live.

26
00:01:40.913 --> 00:01:43.641
Then real users test the MES.

27
00:01:44.442 --> 00:01:46.230
Then comes the cutover weekend.

28
00:01:47.266 --> 00:01:49.437
You use MoSCoW and a cutover plan.

29
00:01:50.491 --> 00:01:55.367
Without this it is unclear what belongs in, and the switchover is improvised.

30
00:01:56.726 --> 00:01:58.398
This is the map of Projects.

31
00:01:59.123 --> 00:02:02.768
The four stations of IT and agile lie side by side.

32
00:02:03.777 --> 00:02:05.356
First Agile and Scrum.

33
00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:09.691
It covers the agile mindset, Scrum, backlog and Kanban.

34
00:02:10.726 --> 00:02:12.909
Then Scaling, SAFe and beyond.

35
00:02:13.682 --> 00:02:17.700
It covers SAFe, portfolio, alternatives and hybrid working.

36
00:02:18.795 --> 00:02:20.594
Then DevOps and delivery.

37
00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.864
It covers the pipeline, DORA, releases and incidents.

38
00:02:25.865 --> 00:02:27.920
Finally Leading IT projects.

39
00:02:28.609 --> 00:02:31.987
It covers requirements, vendor, go-live and testing.

40
00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.848
Each station is a module with four topics.

41
00:02:36.541 --> 00:02:37.853
Start where it hurts.
